# In git tree mode, dup1 and dup2 each delete a four-line block from dup: dup
# leg one block rows 1-4 at lines 11-14 and dup leg two block rows 1-4 at lines
# 9-12. dup1's parent also has two preamble lines at the top and ends with a
# copy of dup rows 06 to 11 whose last line has no final newline. The report
# must pair the two deletions side by side with three lines of context, each
# numbered by its own commit's file, and have no context section, since the tips
# differ only farther from the deletions.
bin: DIFFOFDIFFS
args: --git-tree=repo dup1 dup2
